4. THE COMPLETENESS TEST: does the winning statistic see a LINEAR
   POST-FILTER?  PM_C is a merge that low-passes its own OUTPUT --
   the failure mode the project actually fears.  b2 MEASURED that
   frc2_at_fsig is blind to it by construction (FRC = C/(C+U) with
   both terms scaled by |H|^2).  A statistic that separates blur from
   smoothing but cannot see a post-filter is still useless here.
   The post-filter width is matched to the SAME hp_sd cost, so hp_sd
   cannot tell ANY of the three apart by construction.
